[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Sticky Fingers]
[00:13.38]What two interruptions did the writer have?
[00:20.21]After breakfast, I sent the children to school and then I went to the shops.
[00:27.38]It was still early when I returned home.
[00:31.66]The children were at school, my husband was at work and the house was quiet.
[00:38.24]So I decided to make some meat pies.
[00:42.88]In a short time I was busy mixing butter
[00:46.38]and flour and my hands were soon covered with sticky pastry.
[00:52.80]At exactly that moment, the telephone rang.
[00:57.32]Nothing could have been more annoying.
[01:00.87]I picked up the receiver between two sticky fingers and was dismayed when
[01:07.25]I recognized the voice of Helen Bates.
[01:11.24]It took me ten minutes to persuade her to ring back later. At last I hung up the receiver.
[01:19.02]What a mess! There was pastry on my fingers,
[01:24.37]on the telephone, and on the doorknobs.
[01:28.10]I had no sooner got back to the kitchen than the doorbell rang loud enough to wake the dead.
[01:35.71]This time it was the postman and he wanted me to sign for a registered letter!
